<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>If you're searching for mobile home tie down replacement in Ocala, it's usually because someone else forced the issue. Your insurance company sent a letter asking for tie-down certification, a lender flagged the anchors during financing, or an inspector crawled under the home before closing and found rusted straps. We handle all of it: replacing corroded or loose straps, adding frame and longitudinal anchors, and issuing the certification paperwork that gets insurers and underwriters off your back.</p><p>Marion County sits in Florida Wind Zone II, which means your home needs a specific number of properly rated anchors and straps, not just whatever was installed in 1985. Most full anchoring packages here run $1,500 to $3,000, and a standalone certification inspection is $150 to $300. Call (352) 247-3105 and we'll give you a free written estimate, and if the home also needs work underneath, we can bundle it with <a href="/mobile-home-leveling-ocala/">mobile home leveling</a> in the same visit.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Handle</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What's Included in Every Visit</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E4DCC8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(22,51,44,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Poppins',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16332C;margin:0 0 8px;">Corroded Strap Replacement</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Florida humidity eats galvanized straps from the inside out. We cut out rusted or slack straps and install new corrosion-resistant ones tensioned to spec.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E4DCC8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(22,51,44,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Poppins',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16332C;margin:0 0 8px;">Frame Anchors</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Frame anchors tie your steel I-beams directly to ground anchors and carry most of the wind load. We install and re-tension them to Wind Zone II requirements.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E4DCC8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(22,51,44,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Poppins',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16332C;margin:0 0 8px;">Longitudinal Anchors</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">These resist front-to-back movement and are the piece older installs most often skip. Many homes we inspect in Marion County have none at all.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E4DCC8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(22,51,44,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Poppins',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16332C;margin:0 0 8px;">Full Anchoring Packages</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Complete tear-out and re-anchor jobs typically run $1,500 to $3,000 depending on home size and soil. You get an itemized written quote before we start.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E4DCC8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(22,51,44,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Poppins',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16332C;margin:0 0 8px;">Certification Inspections</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A $150 to $300 inspection with a signed letter documenting your tie-down system for insurers, lenders, and closing agents. Fast turnaround when a deadline is set.</p>
